```javascript
let str = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";
let age = str.match(/\(age \d+\)/)[0];
let result = str.replace(age, "");

console.log(result);
``` 

This JavaScript code will remove the "(age 7)" from the given string. It will work for any number other than 7 in the "(age 7)".

